End-to-end UX overhaul for modern enterprise data teams — engineered an intuitive SQL query builder and interactive visualization engine used by 80k+ analysts.

## The Challenge: Cognitive Overload in Enterprise SQL

At Fortune 500 tech companies, enterprise data teams were bogged down by disparate siloed tools. Product managers, data engineers, and revenue operations analysts spent over 35% of their working hours manually copy-pasting raw SQL snippets across legacy terminals, resolving schema mismatch errors, and parsing unformatted results.

The critical barrier was not data volume — it was *spatial ergonomics*. Complex JOIN relationships spanning hundreds of tables were impossible to visualize mentally, resulting in duplicated engineering hours, high compute costs from unoptimized queries, and significant onboarding delays for junior analysts.

## Architectural Core & Interaction Design

### Visual SQL Builder

Drag-and-drop node canvas that translates schema blocks into performant SQL code bidirectionally in real-time. *Zero syntax failure.*

### Zero-Latency Streaming

Virtualized table renderer capable of sorting and pivoting 500,000 active cell records at 60 frames per second. *Under 16ms render loop.*

### Collaborative Branching

Multiplayer annotations, shared query snippets, and git-like branch exploration built straight into analysis worksheets. *Powered by multiplayer WebSockets.*

## Systematic Accessibility & Density Control

Enterprise power users require intense information density, while exploratory stakeholders demand breathing room. We established an adaptive token system featuring two interchangeable layout modes — **Compact** (32px row heights, mono hierarchy) and **Comfortable** (44px row heights with rich inline visualization pills).

- **Surface 900** — `#0b0f19`
- **Primary Emerald** — `#10b981` (contrast 7.1:1, AAA)
- **Accent Cyan** — `#06b6d4`
- **Alert Amber** — `#f59e0b`
